## Exercise 1 tasks

### Task 1
![](/images/file_move.png){style="width:150px; background:white; border-radius:5px" fig-align="center"}

Change the name of the subdirectory __"four_exercises"__ within your __"Linux"__ directory to __"4_exercises"__.

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Task 1 solution"}
```{bash eval=FALSE}
mv four_exercises 4_exercises
```
:::

### Task 2 {-}
![](/images/backup.png){style="width:150px; background:white; border-radius:5px" fig-align="center"}

Make a backup of the __"4_exercises"__ directory 

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Task 2 solution"}
```{bash eval=FALSE}
cp -r 4_exercises 4_exercises_backup 
```
:::

### Task 3 {-}
![](/images/list_1.png){style="width:150px; background:white; border-radius:5px" fig-align="center"}

List the contents of the __"4_exercises"__ directory

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Task 3 solution"}
```{bash eval=FALSE}
ls 4_exercises
```
:::

### Task 4 {-}
![](/images/print.png){style="width:150px; background:white; border-radius:5px" fig-align="center"}

Within the directory __"4_exercises"__ 

  1. Print the working directory.
  2. Print out to screen the phrase ‘__the echo command allows me to print phrases to screen__’.
  3. Copy the file __"copy_this_file.txt"__ to the directory __"to_me"__ 
  4. Rename the directory __"to_me"__ to __"you"__
  5. Delete the initial __"copy_this_file.txt"__ file

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Task 4 solutions"}
First move into the "4_exercises" directory
```{bash eval=FALSE}
cd 4_exercises
```
Print the working directory
```{bash eval=FALSE}
pwd
```
Print out to screen the phrase ‘the echo command allows me to print phrases to screen’
```{bash eval=FALSE}
echo "the echo command allows me to print phrases to screen"
```
Copy the file copy_this_file.txt to the directory to_me
```{bash eval=FALSE}
cp copy_this_file.txt to_me
```
Rename the directory to_me to you
```{bash eval=FALSE}
mv to_me you
```
Delete the initial copy_this_file.txt file
```{bash eval=FALSE}
rm copy_this_file.txt
```
:::

## Exercise 1 conclusion
![](/images/finish.png){style="width:200px; background: white; border-radius:5px" fig-align="center"}

Brilliant! I hope those tasks helped improve your Linux skills through application.

Please continue onto [Part 2](/part_2/file_reading_and_processing.qmd) and remember you can ask for help and look at the [cheatsheet](/appendix/cheat_sheet.qmd).

